spec.section:
## 6. Readiness gates before dispatch resumes

The replacement MUST remain `recovering`/`read_only` until every mandatory gate is
true and read back from the new controller:

- new writer lease and fence epoch are externally confirmed; old ownership is
  absent or fenced;
- backup manifest, object digests, schema versions, commit markers and sampled
  records verify with no equal-revision conflict;
- `chd` durability sentinel returns the configured achieved durability, not merely
  local `fsync`; the independent backup target is readable;
- configuration/profile/agent/gateway mappings and reattached credential references
  validate by exact generation and scope;
- room heads, ticket/workflow revisions, manifests/attempts, reservations,
  grants/policies, assets and archive indexes complete ordered scans;
- all non-terminal remote runs have a durable reconciliation decision; uncertain or
  unreachable runs have held capacity and an owner/escalation record;
- archive gaps and retention holds are visible, and all cited work/evidence keys
  resolve without treating missing payloads as success;
- scheduler registrations and gateway/capability probes read back successfully;
- a zero-scheduled-trigger assertion proves that readiness checks with no queued
  work and no scheduled fire make no scheduler-caused gateway call; an authorized
  immediate request is a separate controller-admission test; and
- the restore report, incident/audit record and post-restore queries are durable.

Any failed gate leaves dispatch refused and returns a typed failure. It does not
silently discard capacity, recreate work, or claim a successful restore.
